{"id":"8294484f800fb9a1","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-df-saturated.md","title":"Saturated","display":"df-saturated — Saturated","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-saturated","aliases":["58-df-saturated","Saturated"],"display":"df-saturated — Saturated","depends_on":["[[../batch17/58-df-kappa-saturated.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-structure.md]]","[[../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-aleph.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-saturated"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-saturated</span><span>Saturated</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-saturated — Saturated"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"4519dfdd6e3aa4d9\" href=\"?note=4519dfdd6e3aa4d9\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-kappa-saturated.md\">../batch17/58-df-kappa-saturated.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"d9b8711cda3f31ca\" href=\"?note=d9b8711cda3f31ca\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-structure.md\">../batch18/58-df-structure.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"2be08d4ee8aa1590\" href=\"?note=2be08d4ee8aa1590\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md\">../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"535817bf563314f5\" href=\"?note=535817bf563314f5\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-aleph.md\">../batch17/58-df-aleph.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal M,\\kappa\\in V\">\\(\\mathcal M,\\kappa\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Saturated}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Saturated}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Saturated}_S(\\mathcal M,\\kappa)\">\\(\\mathrm{Saturated}_S(\\mathcal M,\\kappa)\\)</span> (canonical predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"4519dfdd6e3aa4d9\" href=\"?note=4519dfdd6e3aa4d9\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-kappa-saturated.md\">../batch17/58-df-kappa-saturated.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Univ}:V\\to V\">\\(\\mathrm{Univ}:V\\to V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)\">\\(\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)\\)</span> (structure universe, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"d9b8711cda3f31ca\" href=\"?note=d9b8711cda3f31ca\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-structure.md\">../batch18/58-df-structure.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|\\cdot|:V\\to V\">\\(|\\cdot|:V\\to V\\)</span> is the cardinality operator and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_0\\in V\">\\(\\aleph_0\\in V\\)</span> is the least infinite cardinal</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Sat}_\\kappa:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\land\\mathrm{Saturated}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Sat}_\\kappa:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\land\\mathrm{Saturated}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (compatibility predicates defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}saturated\\text{-}kappa\\text{-}alias} \\vdash \\mathrm{Sat}_\\kappa(\\mathcal M)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Saturated}_S(\\mathcal M,\\kappa)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}saturated\\text{-}kappa\\text{-}alias} \\vdash \\mathrm{Sat}_\\kappa(\\mathcal M)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Saturated}_S(\\mathcal M,\\kappa)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}saturated\\text{-}cardinality\\text{-}alias} \\vdash \\mathrm{Saturated}(\\mathcal M)\\leftrightarrow|\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)|\\geq\\aleph_0\\land\\mathrm{Saturated}_S(\\mathcal M,|\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)|)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}saturated\\text{-}cardinality\\text{-}alias} \\vdash \\mathrm{Saturated}(\\mathcal M)\\leftrightarrow|\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)|\\geq\\aleph_0\\land\\mathrm{Saturated}_S(\\mathcal M,|\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)|)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A monster model is chosen <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>-saturated and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>-strongly homogeneous for a sufficiently large fixed <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa&gt;|T|\">\\(\\kappa&gt;|T|\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Saturated-model existence at a prescribed cardinal requires hypotheses on the theory and cardinal; GCH alone is not a universal existence theorem.</li>\n<li>The standard real structure <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R_{\\operatorname{an}}\">\\(\\mathbb R_{\\operatorname{an}}\\)</span> is not countably saturated; saturated elementary extensions are used instead.</li>\n<li>The cardinal used by the unary compatibility predicate is obtained from the registered universe and cardinality operators; it is not a typographic size metavariable.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Marker, Model Theory: An Introduction</li>\n<li>Sacks, Saturated Model Theory</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch17/58-df-kappa-saturated.md","status":"resolved","id":"4519dfdd6e3